00:23:58.940 --> 00:24:01.430
so we can use AutoML
Sentiment models

00:24:01.430 --> 00:24:04.280
to predict analyst sentiment
towards those earning

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:05.120
statements.

00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:09.710
We can use AutoML Sentiment
to detect the market sentiment

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:12.860
towards news articles,
or on a lighter note,

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:15.110
you can also use
AutoML Sentiment--

00:24:15.110 --> 00:24:20.070
pun unintended-- to do sentiment
analysis on musical lyrics.

00:24:20.070 --> 00:24:22.680
Let's say there is a
tweet called Delta,

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:26.320
I was waiting on the
tarmac for two hours.

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.410
Now, this is a totally
made up tweet--

00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:31.460
sorry, Delta.

00:24:31.460 --> 00:24:35.300
You may be familiar with
our sentiment analysis API.

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:37.940
Now, if we were to type this
into our sentiment analysis

00:24:37.940 --> 00:24:42.050
API, as you can see, the
sentiment score is neutral.

00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:43.670
Our sentiment
analysis API doesn't

00:24:43.670 --> 00:24:48.490
